1
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:12,700
I searched for myself far away from myself,

2
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:17,200
I saw You, O Truth, in the gardens of my tears.

3
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:21,700
I asked the sun in the sky and the moon in the night,

4
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:26,400
but You were in my heart. Why did I walk so far?

5
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:35,000
I thought I was the sea, yet I longed for a single drop,

6
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:39,600
I thought I understood the world, yet I did not know myself.

7
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:44,100
I read a thousand books, yet missed a single line:

8
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:48,700
"Know yourself." All my life I could not reach those words.

9
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:52,000
Hey! Hey!

10
00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:56,400
O love, set me on fire, let flowers grow from my heart,

11
00:00:56,350 --> 00:01:00,700
let the dust on my soul fall away in one breath.

12
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:05,200
I wanted to reach You, but I lost my way,

13
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:10,400
and the day I let go of my ego, I touched the Truth.

14
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:19,200
Hey! Hey!

15
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:23,600
O heart, a thousand and one worlds are hidden in you,

16
00:01:23,550 --> 00:01:28,800
the day you know yourself, your secret door will open.

17
00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:41,600
I thought it was love, but it was only my ego's desire,

18
00:01:41,550 --> 00:01:46,100
I expected loyalty from others, yet I was unfaithful.

19
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:50,600
I looked for blame in the world and called myself pure,

20
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:55,600
without looking in the mirror, I called myself right.

21
00:01:58,450 --> 00:02:02,900
I beat my head against the stone, I cried to the walls,

22
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:07,600
searching the sky for the Truth, I drifted from my own heart.

23
00:02:07,550 --> 00:02:12,000
For one who cannot conquer himself, a thousand victories are a mirage;

24
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:17,200
the one who conquers his ego is the greatest victor.

25
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:24,700
A candle burns and fades, but its light stays in memory,

26
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:29,400
a person leaves, but his words remain in the traces of good.

27
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:33,700
Why did you hoard wealth? One day it will slip from your hands.

28
00:02:33,650 --> 00:02:38,700
Let your kindness and good name remain on the roads you have walked.

29
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:46,300
Forgive, O man, turn your anger into love,

30
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:50,800
exchange the darkness in your heart for a grain of light.

31
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:55,100
You are a guest in this world, do not claim eternity,

32
00:02:55,050 --> 00:03:00,500
before death comes, O man, do not lose yourself.

